Phase 2: Online Ordering, Pickup (Clover)  [IN PROGRESS]
Design (decided 2026-11-22 after reading Clover docs):
- Clover Hosted Checkout is NOT used: it only takes free-text line items (no inventory items, no modifiers, no Clover tax).
- Flow instead:
  1. Customer builds a cart on our site from LINKED items only (Admin > Clover Links). Options come live from Clover modifier groups.
  2. Server re-prices the cart from Clover (never trusts browser prices) and previews totals + 13% HST:
     POST /v3/merchants/{mId}/atomic_order/checkouts
  3. Card details are entered in Clover's hosted iframe fields (checkout.clover.com/sdk.js, locale en-CA).
     The card never touches our server; we receive a one-time clv_ token.
  4. Server creates the real order: POST /v3/merchants/{mId}/atomic_order/orders
     (inventory item ids + modifiers + orderType "Online Pickup"), then pays it with the
     Ecommerce API: POST https://scl.clover.com/v1/orders/{orderId}/pay (delete_order_on_failure).
  5. Order is saved in Firebase (orders collection); customer sees /order/[id]; kitchen print via print_event if needed.
- Credentials needed (server env only):
  CLOVER_API_TOKEN with Orders READ + WRITE (currently read-only)
  CLOVER_ECOMM_PUBLIC_KEY + CLOVER_ECOMM_PRIVATE_KEY ("Hosted iframe + API/SDK" ecommerce token)
  (No Clover order type is used: owner chose not to add one. Pickup details travel in the order note. CLOVER_ORDER_TYPE_ID is optional.)
- Safety: everything built and tested on a Clover SANDBOX test merchant first
  (apisandbox.dev.clover.com / scl-sandbox.dev.clover.com / checkout.sandbox.dev.clover.com),
  and the public site keeps ordering switched off (ORDERING_ENABLED) until the owner approves.
- Also: open/closed from opening hours + "pause online orders" switch; /admin/orders; confirmation email/SMS.
- To verify while building (docs were ambiguous): modifier id placement in atomic orders, whether a clv_ token
  can be passed straight to /pay, whether online orders print automatically.

